# Test-scoped clang-tidy overrides (merged on top of the repo-root .clang-tidy).
#
# JetPack 7.2 / Ubuntu 24.04 ships clang-tidy 18. Its
# readability-function-cognitive-complexity counts gtest EXPECT_/ASSERT_ macro
# expansions (and the bugprone-unchecked-optional-access `if (!opt){FAIL();return;}`
# guards) markedly higher than clang-tidy 14 did — pushing several linear,
# assertion-list TEST bodies over the threshold even though they were "driven to
# zero" under the 14 baseline. Cognitive complexity is not a meaningful signal for
# a flat sequence of gtest assertions, so the check is disabled for test code ONLY.
# Production code under src/ keeps the full readability-* set (see ../.clang-tidy).
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
